<title>FRANCE: Lagardere makes Thomson-CSF bid.</title>
<headline>Lagardere makes Thomson-CSF bid.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>French conglomerate Lagardere said it filed its bid on Wednesday for defence electronics firm Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>It had the necessary finances for the acquisition and an eventual public offer to buy out Thomson-CSF's minority shareholders if its bid succeeded.</p>
<p>It has cash, bank credit lines and would issue a five billion franc ($859.5 million) bond convertible into Thomson-CSF shares, Lagardere said in a statement. ($ = 5.817 French Francs)</p>
</text>
